            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Vim's impl doesn't really have overlap.\r\n\r\nThe idea seems attractive but why is the impl specialized for mouse wheel input? Wouldn't it apply to arrow keys, etc.? \r\n\r\n> Expensive refreshes slow scrolling\r\n\r\nI've wanted for a long time to see if we can add debounce for syntax, UI callbacks, and other expensive UI work during scrolling. It seems to me that should happen a different layer, not the low-level input layer as in this PR...",
