        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "@justinmk \r\nI’ve generalized the approach to native Normal-mode navigation: mouse wheel, arrows/hjkl, page and half-page commands, Ctrl-E/Ctrl-Y.\r\n  \r\nIn terms of implementation, the input helper now only peeks at the next key and reuses the existing mapping-prefix lookup.\r\n  \r\nThe batching remains in the Normal-mode loop: the higher-level approach is likely quite more work, but might be cleaner, so I can try to investigate it if needed. Do you have some specific idea on how to best approach this?\r\n",
            "created_at": "2026-09-11T06:12:15Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41823#issuecomment-5630281102",
